###The strategy

$\begin{align}
LW&=LA+\blueE{AW}
\\\\
&=3.5+\blueE{AW}
\end{align}$

To find $LW$, we need to find $\blueE{AW}$. We can find $\blueE{AW}$ using a proportion from similar triangles.

###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{\blueE{AW}}{AY}=\dfrac{AY}{AL}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{AW}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{AY}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{AW}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle WAY
\\
{\text{long} \atop \text{leg}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{AW}}{AY}=\dfrac{AY}{AL}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{short} \atop \text{leg}}
\\
&\triangle YAL
\end{array}$

###Finding $LW$

Now that we have $\blueE{AW}$, we can find $LW$.

$\begin{align}
LW&=LA+\blueE{AW}
\\\\
&=3.5+\blueE{14}
\\\\
&=17.5
\end{align}$
